def all_below_threshold(iterable, threshold):
    return all(x < threshold for x in iterable)

Option 2: inclusive or exclusive as needed
- If you want to allow elements equal to the threshold, use <= or < accordingly.

def all_below_or_equal(iterable, threshold):
    return all(x <= threshold for x in iterable)

Option 3: handle non-numeric gracefully (optional)
- Ensures elements are comparable numbers; wrong types will raise by default.

def all_below_threshold_safe(iterable, threshold):
    return all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) and x < threshold for x in iterable)

